# Job Hunter AI — companies file (copy to companies.txt, then add
# `companies_file: "companies.txt"` to config.yaml). One employer per line, with
# no board named: `make resolve` checks each one against every board type
# (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workable) and records where it found a live board in
# data/board_map.yaml, which `make scrape` reads. Blank lines and #-comments are
# ignored (a whole line, or a comment after an entry).
#
#   Name                       # board tokens are guessed from the name
#   Name | alias, alias        # after the bar: extra tokens to try, or careers URLs
#   - <sources line>           # never use this board (for any company)
#
# A plain alias is a board token used exactly as written (Workable accounts are
# case-sensitive); you need one when the token is not the name, e.g. `cba` for
# Commonwealth Bank. A careers URL is a known board for that company, and is how
# a Workday board gets in (its data centre and site cannot be guessed from a name).
#
# Every board found goes live without approval, so check the report `make
# resolve` prints (each new board comes with sample postings). If a token turns
# out to belong to a different company, add a block line for it.
#
# A board listed in sources.txt is pinned: it always wins over the map.
#
# Not sure which employers to list? `make discover` reads the companies in your
# stored Adzuna results and writes them to companies.discovered.txt, with ad
# counts, for you to copy from.

Canva
Atlassian
Commonwealth Bank | cba, https://cba.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CommBank_Careers
Flinders University | flinders
Moody's

# Not the Australian AMP: the token `amp` on Ashby is another company.
- ashby amp
